## Tag / Keyword Rules
Generate a list of 10–15 keywords as a single comma-separated string:
- Blend broad topics (e.g. philosophy, psychology, science, thought experiments, history).
- Blend niche concepts specific to the video's main chapters.
- Include late-night sleep search terms (e.g. sleep philosophy, to fall asleep faster, deep thinking, late night listening).
- Never use clickbait or generic unrelated tags.

## YouTube Thumbnail Text Rules
Generate a 2–10 word ALL-CAPS text hook designed for graphical overlay on the thumbnail.
The hook must tell the viewer what the video is fundamentally ABOUT — topical specificity
beats abstract mystery. A scrolling viewer should know, in a glance, what *kind* of content
they would be sitting with for the next three hours.

Hard constraints:
- Letters, spaces, and (optionally) one leading number only. No punctuation, no emoji.
- Must reflect the actual subject of THIS video. A hook that could apply to any video on the
  channel is too generic — make it fit the topic.

Pick the style that best fits the video's content. Available styles:

- SUPERLATIVE / SCALE: "BIGGEST PHILOSOPHY IDEAS", "DEEPEST PSYCHOLOGY", "DARKEST PHYSICS",
  "OLDEST QUESTIONS".
- TRANSGRESSION: "BANNED IDEAS", "FORBIDDEN THOUGHTS", "HERETICAL THEORIES", "ERASED HISTORY".
- COMPLEXITY / DIFFICULTY: "COMPLEX PHYSICS", "IMPOSSIBLE PARADOXES", "UNSOLVED MYSTERIES".
- CONTROVERSY: "CONTROVERSIAL PHILOSOPHY", "DANGEROUS QUESTIONS", "DISPUTED SCIENCE".
- NUMBERED LIST (preferred when the video title leads with a number): mirror the count and
  compress the topic into 1–5 words. Examples: "40 QUANTUM PARADOXES", "60 BANNED IDEAS",
  "50 BRUTAL TRUTHS", "100 DANGEROUS THOUGHTS", "80 BROKEN BELIEFS".
- PURE CURIOSITY GAP
- or any other that fits the video's specific content and tone

## Tone
Write as if you are a knowledgeable friend recommending something worth watching — warm, confident, and intellectually honest. Never hype or sensationalize.

